From 6f56d542e85425a88803712094a352e0af20e1e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:14:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): Mod double-right-click toggles maximize

A second Mod+right-click on the same window within the double-click
window (300 ms, 8 px slop) applies the opposite maximize state with a
titlebar double-click's target selection: client_maximize picks the
column or the edges for a tiled window, and a floating window fills the
usable area. Clicks past the window stay single clicks and never toggle.
The gesture is opt-in (`[input] mod_right_double_click = "maximize"`);
"none" is the default and keeps the button a pure resize drag.

The pair's first press defers its resize grab until the pointer leaves
the click's slop: beginResize drops the layout's maximize bookkeeping
(the scrolling layout clears the saved width fraction at grab start), so
a grab on the first press would turn the second press's restore into a
re-maximize. The deferral is a grab state (m_grabButton set at press,
MoveGrab::pending's shape) so the release, swallow, isPassthrough() and
reset paths cover it like any interactive operation, and a real drag
promotes it to a grab before the cursor moves.

Two further properties keep the deferred press safe and precise: the
press snapshots its resize edges, because the thirds zones make the
proposal position-sensitive and the pointer has moved by promotion time
(a press that proposes no edges is a plain click), and the layout cancel
hooks drop the press when a layout or axis change would invalidate those
edges. The toggle direction is read at the second press, and the
client-maximize target policy is one implementation shared with
handleRequestMaximize.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
